WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.711
The Southern Cross.

00:02.411 --> 00:07.926
The smallest of the eighty-eight constellations, and the best known south of the equator.

00:08.376 --> 00:14.412
Australia, New Zealand, Brazil, Papua New Guinea and Samoa all fly it on their flags.

00:14.862 --> 00:23.074
The two bright stars beside it are the Pointers, and the nearer is Alpha Centauri, the closest star system to the Sun.

00:23.524 --> 00:30.805
The dark patch at the foot of the Cross is the head of the Emu that Aboriginal Australians see in the Milky Way.
